{# "Historie exportů" dropdown, shared by the single-variant fill page and the
   group fill page: every PINNED version, the most recent unpinned ones
   (ExportHistory::MENU_RECENT) and a link to the full history page, where
   the rest lives. Pinning AND renaming are inline on every row (the pencil
   flips the label into a rename field) and happen IN PLACE: the rows submit
   through Turbo-enabled anchor forms, the answer is a Turbo Stream that
   re-renders the menu body (`_export_history_menu_body.html.twig`, the
   partial that owns `#export-history-menu-body`) while this shell — the
   toggle + the open menu — stays untouched. `data-bs-auto-close="outside"`
   is what keeps the menu open across those clicks. Each row's LINK re-opens
   the page with `?version=<id>`; the controller then seeds the whole fill
   state from that version's snapshot.

   Expects:
   - history:         ExportHistory (pinned + recent split)
   - loaded_version:  null|TemplateExportVersion currently loaded
   - route_name:      the fill page's route
   - route_params:    the fill page's route params (version id gets merged in)
   - history_url:     the dedicated history page
   - redirect_url:    local path a pin / rename returns to (this page) #}
{% if not history.isEmpty %}
    <div class="dropdown d-inline-block">
        <button class="btn btn-outline-secondary dropdown-toggle" type="button" data-bs-toggle="dropdown" data-bs-auto-close="outside" aria-expanded="false">
            <i class="mdi mdi-history"></i> Historie exportů
        </button>
        <div class="dropdown-menu dropdown-menu-end shadow" style="min-width: 24rem; max-height: 28rem; overflow-y: auto;">
            {{ include('_export_history_menu_body.html.twig') }}
        </div>
    </div>
{% endif %}
